### Additional context

This might seem like a weird pattern, but if you've got a dataloader that can return 2 types of data, e.g. (x,y) pairs, and in some cases (x,z,y) triplets, where Z is some additional data, being able to use `isinstance` is a bit safer than checking some other attribute (e.g. len).


